PRETABLE_RERUN -- #538's ONE-INSTRUMENT re-run (fable5, #538 pass 2, F3).  Written 2026-09-18 23:11, BEFORE the re-run;
its mtime is checked against the re-run's frozen instrument.  SAME 17 variant binaries as the first table
(/tmp/gxclose538_bins, md5-checked against logs/bins.md5 before any leg).  The instrument changed in code only by:
(1) the wait-status harness (drain to EOF, reap, `alive' requires a clean exit); (2) l2w16's preset 0x00 -> 0x01;
(3) the dummy-kernel creation.  None of the 16 variants ends the host, so (1) moves no score.
PREDICTIONS: every leg reproduces the first table's SCORE and RED-ROW SET exactly --
    base 13/13; M2_len8 9/13, KILLLEN8 9/13 (all four getenv); vc 10/13 (l0w16, low16, l2w16); vc_ne0 12/13 (l0w16);
    vc_ne1 12/13 (low16); vc_ne2 12/13 (l2w16); vc_ne3 12/13 (wide); vf 10/13 (wide, low16, l2w16); ve 12/13 (low16);
    va vb vg vt1 vt2 vd vh 13/13.
  ONE VALUE CHANGES, BY DESIGN: under a declining variant (M2_len8, KILLLEN8, vc, vc_ne2) `l2w16 getenv' now reads
  0xb1 (the new preset 0x01 | 0xb0), not 0xb0; `l2w16 live' reads 0xb1 on every leg (it is now a real round trip).
  Every session of every leg exits CLEANLY (clean=4/4).
